module

public import StacksFrontier.AlgebraicGeometry.Spaces.ChartDiagramCommonRefinement
public import StacksFrontier.AlgebraicGeometry.Spaces.CoherentAdicPullback
public import StacksFrontier.AlgebraicGeometry.Spaces.PullbackIdealImage

/-!
# Inverse image and ideal-power multiples

Let `g : X ⟶ X'` be a morphism of algebraic spaces over a scheme `S` contained in a big fppf
site `B`, let `𝓘 ⊆ 𝒪_{X'}` be a sheaf of ideals on the small étale site of `X'` and let
`𝓘' = g⁻¹𝓘 · 𝒪_X` be the inverse-image ideal
`AlgebraicGeometry.Space.pullbackIdealImage`.  For an `𝒪_{X'}`-module `M` there are two
subobjects of `g^*M`: the image of `g^*(𝓘 ⁿ M)` and `𝓘' ⁿ (g^*M)`.  **This file proves that they
are killed by the same morphisms out of `g^*M`**, which is
`AlgebraicGeometry.Space.IdealPowerMultipleCompatible` for the inverse image along `g`: the
hypothesis under which the inverse image of coherent adic systems,
`AlgebraicGeometry.Space.coherentAdicPullback`, is defined.

One implication needs only that the unit of `g^* ⊣ g_*` is `𝒪_{X'}`-linear: a morphism out of
`g^*M` which kills `𝓘' ⁿ (g^*M)` kills the image of `g^*(𝓘 ⁿ M)`.  The converse is the
inclusion `𝓘' ⁿ (g^*M) ⊆ image of g^*(𝓘 ⁿ M)`, proved by induction on `n` from the statement that
a section of `𝓘'` carries the image of `g^*(𝓘 ⁿ M)` into the image of `g^*(𝓘 ⁿ⁺¹ M)`.

## Main definitions

* `AlgebraicGeometry.Space.idealPowerUnitSections` — the sections of `g^*M` of product form
  along `𝓘 ⁿ`: restrictions of unit sections `η_d(c • t)` with `c` a section of `𝓘 ⁿ`.
* `AlgebraicGeometry.Space.idealPowerUnitSpan` — the subsheaf of `g^*M` they generate locally.

## Main results

* `AlgebraicGeometry.Space.modulePushforwardCounitApp_ext` — **a section of a direct image is
  determined by its values on the chart diagrams.**
* `AlgebraicGeometry.Space.modulePullbackUnitSection_smul` — the unit section is semilinear over
  pullback of regular functions along the vertical morphism of a chart diagram.
* `AlgebraicGeometry.Space.modulePullback_map_idealPowerMultiple_ι_comp_eq_zero` — a morphism out
  of `g^*M` annihilating `𝓘' ⁿ (g^*M)` annihilates the image of `g^*(𝓘 ⁿ M)`.
* `AlgebraicGeometry.Space.smul_map_unitSection_mem_idealPowerUnitSections` — over a common
  refinement of two chart diagrams, the pullback of a section of `𝓘` times a unit section of
  product form along `𝓘 ⁿ` is one along `𝓘 ⁿ⁺¹`.
* `AlgebraicGeometry.Space.idealPowerMultiple_pullbackIdealImage_le` — `𝓘' ⁿ (g^*M)` lies in the
  subsheaf generated by the sections of product form along `𝓘 ⁿ`.
* `AlgebraicGeometry.Space.idealPowerMultiple_ι_comp_eq_zero_of_modulePullback_map` — **the
  converse implication.**
* `AlgebraicGeometry.Space.idealPowerMultipleCompatible_pullbackIdealImage` — **the inverse image
  along `g` is compatible with the ideal-power multiples of `𝓘` and of `g⁻¹𝓘 · 𝒪_X`.**
* `Stacks.SheafOfModules.smul_mem_localSpan`,
  `Stacks.SheafOfModules.smul_mem_localSpan_of_mem_localImage` — multiplication by a section of
  the structure sheaf, or of a local image in it, between two local spans, checked on generators.

## Implementation notes

The first implication is the argument of the scheme-level
`Stacks.Algebraization.pullback_idealPowerMultiple_comp_eq_zero_iff`, with germs at points
replaced by values on chart diagrams.  A morphism out of `g^*(𝓘 ⁿ M)` is transposed to a morphism
out of `𝓘 ⁿ M`, whose vanishing is, by
`AlgebraicGeometry.Space.idealPowerMultiple_ι_comp_eq_zero_iff`, the vanishing of its values on
the products `r · x` with `r` a section of `𝓘 ⁿ`; such a value is a section of a direct image,
hence determined by its values on the chart diagrams, and those are the values of the original
morphism on the unit sections of the `r · x`.

For the converse both factors of a product `r' · y`, with `r'` a section of `𝓘'` and `y` a section
of `g^*M`, are made explicit locally: `r'` is locally the value of `g^*𝓘 ⟶ 𝒪_X` on a combination of
unit sections, that is a combination of pullbacks `chartDiagramPullback d a` of sections `a` of
`𝓘`, and `y` is locally a combination of restricted unit sections `η_{d'}(s)`.  The two chart
diagrams `d` and `d'` are unrelated, and the identity `chartDiagramPullback e a · η_e(s) =
η_e(a · s)` is about one chart diagram; the common refinement
`AlgebraicGeometry.Space.exists_dominating_chart` supplies a chart diagram `e` over which both
factors are restrictions of values at `e`.  The locality is handled once, on an arbitrary site, by
`Stacks.SheafOfModules.smul_mem_localSpan` and
`Stacks.SheafOfModules.smul_mem_localSpan_of_mem_localImage`, which reduce membership of a
product in a local span to the generators of both factors.

## References

* [Stacks Project, Tag 089P](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/089P)
* [Stacks Project, Tag 0887](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/0887)
* [Stacks Project, Tag 03LU](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/03LU)
-/

@[expose] public noncomputable section

open CategoryTheory Opposite

universe v₁ u₁ u

namespace Stacks.SheafOfModules

/-! ### Local spans and multiplication by local sections -/

variable {C : Type u₁} [Category.{v₁} C] {J : GrothendieckTopology C} {R : Sheaf J RingCat.{u}}
  (N : SheafOfModules.{u} R)

/-- The local span of a family of local sections is monotone in the family. -/
theorem localSpan_mono {T T' : ∀ X : Cᵒᵖ, Set (N.val.obj X)} (h : ∀ X, T X ⊆ T' X) :
    localSpan N T ≤ localSpan N T' := by
  intro X x hx
  refine (mem_localSpan_iff x).2 (J.superset_covering (fun W i hi => ?_)
    ((mem_localSpan_iff x).1 hx))
  have hi' : N.val.restrictₛₗ i.op x ∈ (spanSubmodule N T).obj (op W) := hi
  have hle : (spanSubmodule N T).obj (op W) ≤ (spanSubmodule N T').obj (op W) :=
    Submodule.span_mono (by rintro _ ⟨Z, g, z, hz, e⟩; exact ⟨Z, g, z, h Z hz, e⟩)
  exact hle hi'

/-- **The local span of a family of local sections lies in every sheaf submodule containing the
family**: membership in a sheaf submodule is a local condition, and locally a section of the
local span is a combination of restrictions of members of the family. -/
theorem localSpan_le {T : ∀ X : Cᵒᵖ, Set (N.val.obj X)} {P : N.Submodule}
    (h : ∀ X, T X ⊆ P.obj X) : localSpan N T ≤ P := by
  intro X x hx
  refine P.isSheaf x (J.superset_covering (fun W i hi => ?_) ((mem_localSpan_iff x).1 hx))
  have hi' : N.val.restrictₛₗ i.op x ∈ (spanSubmodule N T).obj (op W) := hi
  have hle : (spanSubmodule N T).obj (op W) ≤ P.obj (op W) :=
    Submodule.span_le.2 (by rintro _ ⟨Z, g, z, hz, rfl⟩; exact P.map_mem g (h Z hz))
  exact hle hi'

/-- **Multiplication by a section of the structure sheaf between two local spans.**  If the
restrictions of `ρ` commute with every section and carry every restriction of a member of `T`
into the span of `T'`, then `ρ` carries the local span of `T` into the local span of `T'`. -/
theorem smul_mem_localSpan {T T' : ∀ X : Cᵒᵖ, Set (N.val.obj X)} {X : Cᵒᵖ} (ρ : R.obj.obj X)
    (hcomm : ∀ {W : C} (a : W ⟶ X.unop) (r : R.obj.obj (op W)),
      R.obj.map a.op ρ * r = r * R.obj.map a.op ρ)
    (hgen : ∀ {W : C} (a : W ⟶ X.unop) {Z : Cᵒᵖ} (h : Z ⟶ op W) {z : N.val.obj Z}, z ∈ T Z →
      R.obj.map a.op ρ • N.val.restrictₛₗ h z ∈ (spanSubmodule N T').obj (op W))
    {x : N.val.obj X} (hx : x ∈ (localSpan N T).obj X) :
    ρ • x ∈ (localSpan N T').obj X := by
  refine (mem_localSpan_iff _).2
    (J.superset_covering (fun W a ha => ?_) ((mem_localSpan_iff x).1 hx))
  replace ha : N.val.restrictₛₗ a.op x ∈ (spanSubmodule N T).obj (op W) := ha
  change N.val.restrictₛₗ a.op (ρ • x) ∈ (spanSubmodule N T').obj (op W)
  rw [map_smulₛₗ]
  generalize N.val.restrictₛₗ a.op x = z at ha ⊢
  induction ha using Submodule.span_induction with
  | mem z hz =>
    obtain ⟨Z, h, z, hz, rfl⟩ := hz
    exact hgen a h hz
  | zero =>
    rw [smul_zero]
    exact Submodule.zero_mem _
  | add z z' _ _ hz hz' =>
    rw [smul_add]
    exact Submodule.add_mem _ hz hz'
  | smul r z _ hz =>
    rw [smul_smul, hcomm a r, mul_smul]
    exact Submodule.smul_mem _ r hz

/-- **Multiplication by a section of a local image between two local spans.**  Let
`ψ : K ⟶ R` be a morphism into the structure sheaf whose source is the local span of a family
`U`.  If every value of `ψ` on a restriction of a member of `U` carries the local span of `T`
into the local span of `T'`, then so does every section of the local image of `ψ`. -/
theorem smul_mem_localSpan_of_mem_localImage {K : SheafOfModules.{u} R}
    (ψ : K ⟶ SheafOfModules.unit R) (U : ∀ X : Cᵒᵖ, Set (K.val.obj X))
    (hU : ∀ (X : Cᵒᵖ) (w : K.val.obj X), w ∈ (localSpan K U).obj X)
    {T T' : ∀ X : Cᵒᵖ, Set (N.val.obj X)}
    (hgen : ∀ {W : C} {Z : Cᵒᵖ} (h : Z ⟶ op W) {u : K.val.obj Z}, u ∈ U Z →
      ∀ ρ : R.obj.obj (op W), ρ = ψ.val.app (op W) (K.val.restrictₛₗ h u) →
      ∀ y ∈ (localSpan N T).obj (op W), ρ • y ∈ (localSpan N T').obj (op W))
    {X : Cᵒᵖ} {r : R.obj.obj X} (hr : r ∈ (localImage ψ.val).obj X)
    {y : N.val.obj X} (hy : y ∈ (localSpan N T).obj X) :
    r • y ∈ (localSpan N T').obj X := by
  refine (localSpan N T').isSheaf (r • y) (J.transitive hr _ fun V a ha => ?_)
  obtain ⟨w₀, hw₀⟩ := ha
  refine J.superset_covering (fun V' b hb => ?_) ((mem_localSpan_iff w₀).1 (hU _ w₀))
  replace hb : K.val.restrictₛₗ b.op w₀ ∈ (spanSubmodule K U).obj (op V') := hb
  change N.val.restrictₛₗ (b ≫ a).op (r • y) ∈ (localSpan N T').obj (op V')
  have hy' : N.val.restrictₛₗ (b ≫ a).op y ∈ (localSpan N T).obj (op V') :=
    (localSpan N T).map_mem _ hy
  have hρ : R.obj.map (b ≫ a).op r = ψ.val.app (op V') (K.val.restrictₛₗ b.op w₀) := by
    rw [PresheafOfModules.restrictₛₗ_apply, PresheafOfModules.naturality_apply, hw₀, op_comp,
      Functor.map_comp, ConcreteCategory.comp_apply]
    rfl
  rw [map_smulₛₗ]
  change R.obj.map (b ≫ a).op r • _ ∈ _
  generalize R.obj.map (b ≫ a).op r = ρ at hρ ⊢
  generalize N.val.restrictₛₗ (b ≫ a).op y = y' at hy' ⊢
  generalize K.val.restrictₛₗ b.op w₀ = w at hb hρ
  induction hb using Submodule.span_induction generalizing ρ with
  | mem w hw =>
    obtain ⟨Z, h, u, hu, rfl⟩ := hw
    exact hgen h hu ρ hρ y' hy'
  | zero =>
    obtain rfl : ρ = 0 := hρ.trans (map_zero _)
    rw [zero_smul]
    exact Submodule.zero_mem _
  | add w w' _ _ hw hw' =>
    obtain ⟨ρ₁, hρ₁⟩ : ∃ ρ₁ : R.obj.obj (op V'), ρ₁ = ψ.val.app (op V') w := ⟨_, rfl⟩
    obtain ⟨ρ₂, hρ₂⟩ : ∃ ρ₂ : R.obj.obj (op V'), ρ₂ = ψ.val.app (op V') w' := ⟨_, rfl⟩
    obtain rfl : ρ = ρ₁ + ρ₂ := hρ.trans ((map_add _ _ _).trans (by subst hρ₁ hρ₂; rfl))
    rw [add_smul]
    exact Submodule.add_mem _ (hw ρ₁ hρ₁) (hw' ρ₂ hρ₂)
  | smul c w _ hw =>
    obtain ⟨ρ₁, hρ₁⟩ : ∃ ρ₁ : R.obj.obj (op V'), ρ₁ = ψ.val.app (op V') w := ⟨_, rfl⟩
    obtain rfl : ρ = c * ρ₁ := hρ.trans ((map_smul _ c w).trans (by subst hρ₁; rfl))
    rw [mul_smul]
    exact Submodule.smul_mem _ c (hw ρ₁ hρ₁)

end Stacks.SheafOfModules

namespace AlgebraicGeometry.Space

variable (B : BigFppfSite.{u}) (S : Scheme.{u}) (hS : B.Contains S)
    {X X' : AlgebraicSpaces B S hS} (g : X ⟶ X')

/-! ### Sections of a direct image are determined on chart diagrams -/

/-- **A section of a direct image is determined by its values on the chart diagrams.**  The
sections of `g_*F` over an étale chart `V` of `X'` are a limit over the étale scheme charts of
`X` above `X ×_{X'} V`, and those charts are exactly the chart diagrams over `V`. -/
theorem modulePushforwardCounitApp_ext (F : Modules.{u, u} B S hS X.1 X.2)
    (V : SmallEtale B S hS X'.1)
    {x y : ((modulePushforward B S hS g).obj F).val.obj (op V)}
    (h : ∀ j : StructuredArrow (op (chartBaseChange B S hS g V))
        (comparisonFunctor B S hS X).op,
      modulePushforwardCounitApp B S hS g F (chartDiagramOfIndex B S hS g V j) x =
        modulePushforwardCounitApp B S hS g F (chartDiagramOfIndex B S hS g V j) y) :
    x = y := by
  refine moduleChartProjection_ext B S hS g V (moduleSetSheaf B S hS X F) fun j => ?_
  rw [← indexOfChartDiagram_chartDiagramOfIndex B S hS g V j]
  exact h j

/-! ### The unit section is semilinear -/

/-- The unit section of a module pullback is the value at a chart diagram of the chartwise
transpose of the identity. -/
theorem modulePullbackHomFMap_id_app (M : Modules.{u, u} B S hS X'.1 X'.2)
    (d : ChartDiagram B S hS X.1 X'.1 g.hom) (s : M.val.obj (op d.V)) :
    (modulePullbackHomFMap B S hS g M ((modulePullback B S hS g).obj M) (𝟙 _)).app d s =
      modulePullbackUnitSection B S hS g M d s :=
  modulePullbackHomFMap_app B S hS g M ((modulePullback B S hS g).obj M) (𝟙 _) d s

/-- **The unit section is semilinear over pullback of regular functions.**  On a commutative
diagram `d` of étale scheme charts, the unit section of `r · s` is the pullback of `r` along the
vertical morphism of `d`, acting on the unit section of `s`.  This is the semilinearity of the
chartwise transpose of the identity of `g^*M`. -/
theorem modulePullbackUnitSection_smul (M : Modules.{u, u} B S hS X'.1 X'.2)
    (d : ChartDiagram B S hS X.1 X'.1 g.hom)
    (r : ((Stacks.SheafOfModules.Tensor.ringSheaf
      (smallEtaleRingedSite B S hS X'.1 X'.2).O)).obj.obj (op d.V))
    (s : M.val.obj (op d.V)) :
    modulePullbackUnitSection B S hS g M d (r • s) =
      chartDiagramPullback B S hS g d r • modulePullbackUnitSection B S hS g M d s :=
  ((modulePullbackHomFMap_id_app B S hS g M d (r • s)).symm.trans
    ((modulePullbackHomFMap B S hS g M ((modulePullback B S hS g).obj M)
      (𝟙 _)).map_smul d r s)).trans
    (congrArg (fun z : ((modulePullback B S hS g).obj M).val.obj (op d.U) =>
        chartDiagramPullback B S hS g d r • z) (modulePullbackHomFMap_id_app B S hS g M d s))

/-! ### Vanishing of a morphism out of an inverse image -/

/-- The adjoint transpose of a zero morphism vanishes. -/
theorem homEquiv_zero (P : Modules.{u, u} B S hS X'.1 X'.2)
    (N : Modules.{u, u} B S hS X.1 X.2) :
    (modulePullbackAdjunction B S hS g).homEquiv P N 0 = 0 := by
  rw [Adjunction.homEquiv_unit, Functor.map_zero, Limits.comp_zero]

/-- **A morphism out of an inverse image vanishes as soon as its adjoint transpose does.**  For
a morphism `a : P ⟶ M` of `𝒪_{X'}`-modules and `φ` out of `g^*M`, the composite `g^*a ≫ φ`
vanishes exactly when the composite of `a` with the adjoint transpose of `φ` does; this is the
direction that is used. -/
theorem modulePullback_map_comp_eq_zero {P M : Modules.{u, u} B S hS X'.1 X'.2}
    {N : Modules.{u, u} B S hS X.1 X.2} (a : P ⟶ M)
    (φ : (modulePullback B S hS g).obj M ⟶ N)
    (h : a ≫ (modulePullbackAdjunction B S hS g).homEquiv M N φ = 0) :
    (modulePullback B S hS g).map a ≫ φ = 0 :=
  ((modulePullbackAdjunction B S hS g).homEquiv P N).injective
    ((((modulePullbackAdjunction B S hS g).homEquiv_naturality_left a φ).trans h).trans
      (homEquiv_zero B S hS g P N).symm)

/-! ### The implication -/

variable (𝓘 : (SheafOfModules.unit
  ((Stacks.SheafOfModules.Tensor.ringSheaf (smallEtaleRingedSite B S hS X'.1 X'.2).O))).Submodule)

/-- The adjoint transpose of a morphism out of `g^*M` kills a product `r · x` with `r` a section
of `𝓘 ⁿ`, as soon as the morphism kills `𝓘' ⁿ (g^*M)`.

The value of the transpose on `r · x` is a section of a direct image, so it is determined by its
values on the chart diagrams; on a chart diagram those values are the values of the morphism on
the unit sections, the unit section of `r · x` is the pullback of `r` acting on the unit section
of `x`, and the pullback of `r` is a section of `𝓘' ⁿ`. -/
theorem homEquiv_app_smul_eq_zero (n : ℕ) (M : Modules.{u, u} B S hS X'.1 X'.2)
    {N : Modules.{u, u} B S hS X.1 X.2} (φ : (modulePullback B S hS g).obj M ⟶ N)
    (h : (idealPowerMultiple B S hS X.1 X.2 (pullbackIdealImage B S hS g 𝓘) n
      ((modulePullback B S hS g).obj M)).ι ≫ φ = 0)
    (V : SmallEtale B S hS X'.1) {r : chartRing B S hS X'.1 X'.2 V}
    (hr : r ∈ chartIdeal B S hS X' 𝓘 V ^ n) (x : M.val.obj (op V)) :
    ((modulePullbackAdjunction B S hS g).homEquiv M N φ).val.app (op V) (r • x) = 0 := by
  have hφ := (idealPowerMultiple_ι_comp_eq_zero_iff B S hS X.1 X.2
    (pullbackIdealImage B S hS g 𝓘) n φ).mp h
  refine modulePushforwardCounitApp_ext B S hS g N V fun j => ?_
  have hzero : modulePushforwardCounitApp B S hS g N (chartDiagramOfIndex B S hS g V j) 0 = 0 := by
    have h := modulePushforwardCounitApp_add B S hS g N (chartDiagramOfIndex B S hS g V j) 0 0
    rw [add_zero] at h
    exact (add_left_cancel
      (a := modulePushforwardCounitApp B S hS g N (chartDiagramOfIndex B S hS g V j) 0) (b := 0)
      (by rw [add_zero]; exact h)).symm
  refine Eq.trans ?_ hzero.symm
  refine (modulePullbackHomFMap_app B S hS g M N φ
    (chartDiagramOfIndex B S hS g V j) (r • x)).trans ?_
  refine Eq.trans (congrArg (φ.val.app (op (chartDiagramOfIndex B S hS g V j).U))
    (modulePullbackUnitSection_smul B S hS g M (chartDiagramOfIndex B S hS g V j) r x)) ?_
  exact hφ (chartDiagramOfIndex B S hS g V j).U
    (chartDiagramPullback B S hS g (chartDiagramOfIndex B S hS g V j) r)
    (chartDiagramPullback_pow_mem_chartIdeal_pullbackIdealImage B S hS g 𝓘 n
      (chartDiagramOfIndex B S hS g V j) hr)
    (modulePullbackUnitSection B S hS g M (chartDiagramOfIndex B S hS g V j) x)

/-- **A morphism out of `g^*M` annihilating `𝓘' ⁿ (g^*M)` annihilates the image of
`g^*(𝓘 ⁿ M)`**, for `𝓘' = g⁻¹𝓘 · 𝒪_X` the inverse-image ideal.  This is one implication of
`AlgebraicGeometry.Space.IdealPowerMultipleCompatible` for the inverse image along an arbitrary
morphism of algebraic spaces; the converse is not proved here. -/
theorem modulePullback_map_idealPowerMultiple_ι_comp_eq_zero (n : ℕ)
    (M : Modules.{u, u} B S hS X'.1 X'.2) {N : Modules.{u, u} B S hS X.1 X.2}
    (φ : (modulePullback B S hS g).obj M ⟶ N)
    (h : (idealPowerMultiple B S hS X.1 X.2 (pullbackIdealImage B S hS g 𝓘) n
      ((modulePullback B S hS g).obj M)).ι ≫ φ = 0) :
    (modulePullback B S hS g).map (idealPowerMultiple B S hS X'.1 X'.2 𝓘 n M).ι ≫ φ = 0 :=
  modulePullback_map_comp_eq_zero B S hS g (idealPowerMultiple B S hS X'.1 X'.2 𝓘 n M).ι φ
    ((idealPowerMultiple_ι_comp_eq_zero_iff B S hS X'.1 X'.2 𝓘 n
        ((modulePullbackAdjunction B S hS g).homEquiv M N φ)).mpr
      fun V _ hr x => homEquiv_app_smul_eq_zero B S hS g 𝓘 n M φ h V hr x)

/-! ### The converse implication -/

section Converse

variable (M : Modules.{u, u} B S hS X'.1 X'.2)

/-- The local sections of `g^*M` of product form along `𝓘 ⁿ`: over an étale chart `W` of `X`,
the restrictions to `W` of the unit sections `η_d(c • t)`, for `d` a chart diagram, `c` a
section of `𝓘 ⁿ` and `t` a section of `M`, both over the chart of `X'` of `d`. -/
def idealPowerUnitSections (n : ℕ) (W : (SmallEtale B S hS X.1)ᵒᵖ) :
    Set (((modulePullback B S hS g).obj M).val.obj W) :=
  {y | ∃ (d : ChartDiagram B S hS X.1 X'.1 g.hom) (i : W.unop ⟶ d.U)
    (c : chartRing B S hS X'.1 X'.2 d.V) (t : M.val.obj (op d.V)),
    c ∈ chartIdeal B S hS X' 𝓘 d.V ^ n ∧
      ((modulePullback B S hS g).obj M).val.map i.op
        (modulePullbackUnitSection B S hS g M d (c • t)) = y}

/-- The subsheaf of `g^*M` of the sections lying locally in the span of the sections of
product form along `𝓘 ⁿ`, `AlgebraicGeometry.Space.idealPowerUnitSections`.  It is the image of
`g^*(𝓘 ⁿ M)` in `g^*M`, described through generators. -/
abbrev idealPowerUnitSpan (n : ℕ) : ((modulePullback B S hS g).obj M).Submodule :=
  Stacks.SheafOfModules.localSpan ((modulePullback B S hS g).obj M)
    (idealPowerUnitSections B S hS g 𝓘 M n)

/-- **Over a common refinement of two chart diagrams, a pullback of a section of `𝓘` times a
unit section of product form along `𝓘 ⁿ` is a unit section of product form along `𝓘 ⁿ⁺¹`.**

The two chart diagrams `d` and `d'` are dominated, over the chart `Z` of `X`, by a third one
(`AlgebraicGeometry.Space.exists_dominating_chart`); over it both the pullback of `s` and the
unit section of `c • t` are restrictions of values at one chart diagram, and there the unit
section is semilinear (`AlgebraicGeometry.Space.modulePullbackUnitSection_smul`). -/
theorem smul_map_unitSection_mem_idealPowerUnitSections (n : ℕ)
    (d d' : ChartDiagram B S hS X.1 X'.1 g.hom) {Z : SmallEtale B S hS X.1}
    (k : Z ⟶ d.U) (i : Z ⟶ d'.U)
    {s : chartRing B S hS X'.1 X'.2 d.V} (hs : s ∈ chartIdeal B S hS X' 𝓘 d.V)
    {c : chartRing B S hS X'.1 X'.2 d'.V} (hc : c ∈ chartIdeal B S hS X' 𝓘 d'.V ^ n)
    (t : M.val.obj (op d'.V)) {y : ((modulePullback B S hS g).obj M).val.obj (op Z)}
    (hy : ((modulePullback B S hS g).obj M).val.map i.op
      (modulePullbackUnitSection B S hS g M d' (c • t)) = y) :
    chartRestrict (hF := X.2) k (chartDiagramPullback B S hS g d s) • y ∈
      idealPowerUnitSections B S hS g 𝓘 M (n + 1) (op Z) := by
  subst hy
  obtain ⟨W, g', hc', p, q, hp, hq⟩ := exists_dominating_chart B S hS g d d' k i
  have h1 : chartDiagramPullback B S hS g ⟨Z, W, g', hc'⟩ (chartRestrict (hF := X'.2) p s) =
      chartRestrict (hF := X.2) k (chartDiagramPullback B S hS g d s) :=
    (structureModuleFMap B S hS g).naturality d ⟨Z, W, g', hc'⟩ k p hp s
  have h2 : modulePullbackUnitSection B S hS g M ⟨Z, W, g', hc'⟩ (M.val.map q.op (c • t)) =
      ((modulePullback B S hS g).obj M).val.map i.op
        (modulePullbackUnitSection B S hS g M d' (c • t)) :=
    (modulePullbackHomFMap_id_app B S hS g M ⟨Z, W, g', hc'⟩ _).symm.trans
      (((modulePullbackHomFMap B S hS g M ((modulePullback B S hS g).obj M)
        (𝟙 _)).naturality d' ⟨Z, W, g', hc'⟩ i q hq (c • t)).trans
        (congrArg (fun y => ((modulePullback B S hS g).obj M).val.map i.op y)
          (modulePullbackHomFMap_id_app B S hS g M d' (c • t))))
  refine ⟨⟨Z, W, g', hc'⟩, 𝟙 Z,
    chartRestrict (hF := X'.2) p s * chartRestrict (hF := X'.2) q c, M.val.map q.op t, ?_, ?_⟩
  · rw [pow_succ']
    exact Ideal.mul_mem_mul (𝓘.map_mem p.op hs)
      (chartRestrict_mem_chartIdeal_pow B S hS X'.1 X'.2 𝓘 q n hc)
  · refine (restrictₛₗ_id B S hS X.1 X.2 ((modulePullback B S hS g).obj M) _).trans ?_
    rw [← h1, ← h2]
    refine (congrArg (modulePullbackUnitSection B S hS g M ⟨Z, W, g', hc'⟩)
      (mul_smul _ _ _)).trans ((modulePullbackUnitSection_smul B S hS g M _ _ _).trans ?_)
    exact congrArg _ (congrArg _ (PresheafOfModules.map_smul M.val q.op c t).symm)

/-- **A pullback of a section of `𝓘`, restricted to an étale chart of `X`, carries the image of
`g^*(𝓘 ⁿ M)` into the image of `g^*(𝓘 ⁿ⁺¹ M)`.**  Membership in either image is local, and
locally a section of the first is a combination of sections of product form along `𝓘 ⁿ`, each of
which the pullback carries to one of product form along `𝓘 ⁿ⁺¹` by
`AlgebraicGeometry.Space.smul_map_unitSection_mem_idealPowerUnitSections`. -/
theorem smul_mem_idealPowerUnitSpan_succ (n : ℕ) (d : ChartDiagram B S hS X.1 X'.1 g.hom)
    {V : SmallEtale B S hS X.1} (k : V ⟶ d.U)
    {s : chartRing B S hS X'.1 X'.2 d.V} (hs : s ∈ chartIdeal B S hS X' 𝓘 d.V)
    {y : ((modulePullback B S hS g).obj M).val.obj (op V)}
    (hy : y ∈ (idealPowerUnitSpan B S hS g 𝓘 M n).obj (op V)) :
    chartRestrict (hF := X.2) k (chartDiagramPullback B S hS g d s) • y ∈
      (idealPowerUnitSpan B S hS g 𝓘 M (n + 1)).obj (op V) := by
  refine Stacks.SheafOfModules.smul_mem_localSpan _ _ (fun a r => mul_comm _ _)
    (fun {W} a {Z} h {z} hz => ?_) hy
  obtain ⟨d₀, i₀, c, t, hc, rfl⟩ := hz
  have hρ : (Stacks.SheafOfModules.Tensor.ringSheaf
      (smallEtaleRingedSite B S hS X.1 X.2).O).obj.map a.op
        (chartRestrict (hF := X.2) k (chartDiagramPullback B S hS g d s)) =
      chartRestrict (hF := X.2) (a ≫ k) (chartDiagramPullback B S hS g d s) := by
    have hc := (Stacks.SheafOfModules.Tensor.ringSheaf
      (smallEtaleRingedSite B S hS X.1 X.2).O).obj.map_comp k.op a.op
    exact (congrArg (fun φ => RingCat.Hom.hom φ (chartDiagramPullback B S hS g d s)) hc).symm
  rw [hρ]
  exact Stacks.SheafOfModules.mem_spanSubmodule
    (smul_map_unitSection_mem_idealPowerUnitSections B S hS g 𝓘 M n d d₀ (a ≫ k)
      (h.unop ≫ i₀) hs hc t (PresheafOfModules.map_comp_apply _ _ _ _))

/-- **A section of `g⁻¹𝓘 · 𝒪_X` carries the image of `g^*(𝓘 ⁿ M)` into the image of
`g^*(𝓘 ⁿ⁺¹ M)`.**  A section of `g⁻¹𝓘 · 𝒪_X` is locally the value of `g^*𝓘 ⟶ 𝒪_X` on a section
of `g^*𝓘`, which is locally a combination of unit sections, and the value on a unit section is
a pullback of a section of `𝓘` (`AlgebraicGeometry.Space.pullbackIdealHom_unitSection`); so this
is `AlgebraicGeometry.Space.smul_mem_idealPowerUnitSpan_succ` assembled by
`Stacks.SheafOfModules.smul_mem_localSpan_of_mem_localImage`. -/
theorem smul_mem_idealPowerUnitSpan_succ_of_mem_pullbackIdealImage (n : ℕ)
    {W : SmallEtale B S hS X.1} {r : chartRing B S hS X.1 X.2 W}
    (hr : r ∈ chartIdeal B S hS X (pullbackIdealImage B S hS g 𝓘) W)
    {y : ((modulePullback B S hS g).obj M).val.obj (op W)}
    (hy : y ∈ (idealPowerUnitSpan B S hS g 𝓘 M n).obj (op W)) :
    r • y ∈ (idealPowerUnitSpan B S hS g 𝓘 M (n + 1)).obj (op W) := by
  refine Stacks.SheafOfModules.smul_mem_localSpan_of_mem_localImage _
    (pullbackIdealHom B S hS g 𝓘) (modulePullbackUnitSections B S hS g 𝓘.toSheafOfModules)
    (mem_localModulePullbackUnitSpan B S hS g 𝓘.toSheafOfModules)
    (fun {V} {Z} h {u} hu ρ hρ y' hy' => ?_) hr hy
  obtain ⟨d, i, a, rfl⟩ := hu
  have h1 := PresheafOfModules.naturality_apply (pullbackIdealHom B S hS g 𝓘).val (i.op ≫ h)
    (modulePullbackUnitSection B S hS g 𝓘.toSheafOfModules d a)
  have h2 : (pullbackIdealHom B S hS g 𝓘).val.app (op d.U)
      (modulePullbackUnitSection B S hS g 𝓘.toSheafOfModules d a) =
      chartDiagramPullback B S hS g d (𝓘.ι.val.app (op d.V) a) :=
    pullbackIdealHom_unitSection B S hS g 𝓘 d a
  have hρ' : ρ = chartRestrict (hF := X.2) (h.unop ≫ i)
      (chartDiagramPullback B S hS g d (𝓘.ι.val.app (op d.V) a)) :=
    hρ.trans ((congrArg ((pullbackIdealHom B S hS g 𝓘).val.app (op V))
      (PresheafOfModules.map_comp_apply _ _ _ _).symm).trans (h1.trans (congrArg _ h2)))
  subst hρ'
  exact smul_mem_idealPowerUnitSpan_succ B S hS g 𝓘 M n d (h.unop ≫ i) a.2 hy'

/-- Every section of `g^*M` lies in the image of `g^*(𝓘 ⁰ M)`: the unit sections generate
`g^*M` locally (`AlgebraicGeometry.Space.mem_localModulePullbackUnitSpan`), and a unit section
`η_d(t)` is the one of product form `η_d(1 • t)`. -/
theorem mem_idealPowerUnitSpan_zero {W : (SmallEtale B S hS X.1)ᵒᵖ}
    (y : ((modulePullback B S hS g).obj M).val.obj W) :
    y ∈ (idealPowerUnitSpan B S hS g 𝓘 M 0).obj W := by
  refine Stacks.SheafOfModules.localSpan_mono _ (fun W' z hz => ?_) W
    (mem_localModulePullbackUnitSpan B S hS g M W y)
  obtain ⟨d, i, t, rfl⟩ := hz
  refine ⟨d, i, 1, t, ?_, ?_⟩
  · rw [pow_zero, Ideal.one_eq_top]
    exact Submodule.mem_top
  · rw [one_smul]

/-- **A morphism out of `g^*M` killing the image of `g^*(𝓘 ⁿ M)` kills the subsheaf generated
by the sections of product form along `𝓘 ⁿ`.**  Its adjoint transpose kills `𝓘 ⁿ M`, and its
value on a unit section `η_d(c • t)` is the value of the chartwise transpose at `c • t`, which is
a section of `𝓘 ⁿ M`. -/
theorem idealPowerUnitSpan_le_ker (n : ℕ) {N : Modules.{u, u} B S hS X.1 X.2}
    (φ : (modulePullback B S hS g).obj M ⟶ N)
    (h : (modulePullback B S hS g).map (idealPowerMultiple B S hS X'.1 X'.2 𝓘 n M).ι ≫ φ = 0) :
    idealPowerUnitSpan B S hS g 𝓘 M n ≤ SheafOfModules.Submodule.ker φ := by
  have hι : (idealPowerMultiple B S hS X'.1 X'.2 𝓘 n M).ι ≫
      (modulePullbackAdjunction B S hS g).homEquiv M N φ = 0 :=
    ((modulePullbackAdjunction B S hS g).homEquiv_naturality_left _ φ).symm.trans
      ((congrArg _ h).trans (homEquiv_zero B S hS g _ N))
  refine Stacks.SheafOfModules.localSpan_le _ fun W y hy => ?_
  obtain ⟨d, i, c, t, hc, rfl⟩ := hy
  have hmem : c • t ∈ (idealPowerMultiple B S hS X'.1 X'.2 𝓘 n M).obj (op d.V) :=
    le_idealPowerMultiple_obj B S hS X'.1 X'.2 𝓘 n M d.V
      (Submodule.smul_mem_smul hc Submodule.mem_top)
  have h0 : φ.val.app (op d.U) (modulePullbackUnitSection B S hS g M d (c • t)) = 0 := by
    refine (modulePullbackHomFMap_app B S hS g M N φ d (c • t)).symm.trans ?_
    refine (modulePushforwardHomEquiv_app_comp_left B S hS g
      (idealPowerMultiple B S hS X'.1 X'.2 𝓘 n M).ι
      ((modulePullbackAdjunction B S hS g).homEquiv M N φ) d ⟨c • t, hmem⟩).symm.trans ?_
    rw [hι]
    exact modulePushforwardHomEquiv_zero_app B S hS g N _ d _
  exact (SheafOfModules.Submodule.mem_ker φ W _).2
    ((PresheafOfModules.naturality_apply φ.val i.op _).trans
      ((congrArg _ h0).trans (map_zero _)))

/-- **The `n`-th power of `g⁻¹𝓘 · 𝒪_X` times `g^*M` lies in the image of `g^*(𝓘 ⁿ M)`**,
described through generators.  Induction on `n`, the step being
`AlgebraicGeometry.Space.smul_mem_idealPowerUnitSpan_succ_of_mem_pullbackIdealImage`. -/
theorem idealPowerMultiple_pullbackIdealImage_le (n : ℕ) :
    idealPowerMultiple B S hS X.1 X.2 (pullbackIdealImage B S hS g 𝓘) n
      ((modulePullback B S hS g).obj M) ≤ idealPowerUnitSpan B S hS g 𝓘 M n := by
  rw [idealPowerMultiple_le_iff]
  intro W
  induction n with
  | zero => exact fun y _ => mem_idealPowerUnitSpan_zero B S hS g 𝓘 M y
  | succ n ih =>
    rw [pow_succ', Submodule.mul_smul]
    exact Submodule.smul_le.2 fun r hr y hy =>
      smul_mem_idealPowerUnitSpan_succ_of_mem_pullbackIdealImage B S hS g 𝓘 M n hr (ih hy)

/-- **A morphism out of `g^*M` annihilating the image of `g^*(𝓘 ⁿ M)` annihilates
`𝓘' ⁿ (g^*M)`**, for `𝓘' = g⁻¹𝓘 · 𝒪_X` the inverse-image ideal.  This is the converse of
`AlgebraicGeometry.Space.modulePullback_map_idealPowerMultiple_ι_comp_eq_zero`. -/
theorem idealPowerMultiple_ι_comp_eq_zero_of_modulePullback_map (n : ℕ)
    {N : Modules.{u, u} B S hS X.1 X.2} (φ : (modulePullback B S hS g).obj M ⟶ N)
    (h : (modulePullback B S hS g).map (idealPowerMultiple B S hS X'.1 X'.2 𝓘 n M).ι ≫ φ = 0) :
    (idealPowerMultiple B S hS X.1 X.2 (pullbackIdealImage B S hS g 𝓘) n
      ((modulePullback B S hS g).obj M)).ι ≫ φ = 0 :=
  (submodule_ι_comp_eq_zero_iff B S hS X.1 X.2 _ φ).2
    ((idealPowerMultiple_pullbackIdealImage_le B S hS g 𝓘 M n).trans
      (idealPowerUnitSpan_le_ker B S hS g 𝓘 M n φ h))

end Converse

/-- **The inverse image along `g` is compatible with the ideal-power multiples of `𝓘` and of the
inverse-image ideal `g⁻¹𝓘 · 𝒪_X`**: a morphism out of `g^*M` kills the image of `g^*(𝓘 ⁿ M)`
exactly when it kills `(g⁻¹𝓘 · 𝒪_X) ⁿ (g^*M)`.  This is the hypothesis under which
`AlgebraicGeometry.Space.coherentAdicPullback` is defined, discharged for the inverse-image ideal
of an arbitrary morphism of algebraic spaces. -/
theorem idealPowerMultipleCompatible_pullbackIdealImage :
    IdealPowerMultipleCompatible B S hS (modulePullback B S hS g) 𝓘
      (pullbackIdealImage B S hS g 𝓘) := fun n M _ φ =>
  ⟨idealPowerMultiple_ι_comp_eq_zero_of_modulePullback_map B S hS g 𝓘 M n φ,
    modulePullback_map_idealPowerMultiple_ι_comp_eq_zero B S hS g 𝓘 n M φ⟩

end AlgebraicGeometry.Space

end
